I think Jorge is right that ve'i sequences are like sets.  I think
we might want to consider:
perhaps what would be best would be to take therespectively joi operator and
 move it to LAhE, in which case it would
only require "ce" between terms inside.

The advantage is a clearer and simpler use of the respectively operator.

On the other hand, in writing this, I suddenly realize that this would
eliminate the ability to use "respectively" in selbri (e.g. jack and jill,
respectively walked and ran up the hill.), so perhaps this would not
be a good idea.

